 # Night cicada ambience, 2026-10-09
 
+Current master (2026-10-10): a 40-second recording with a four-second equal-power blend replaces the original 18-second loop. See the follow-up below. The original delivery receipts remain historical evidence.
+
 SND19: owner-requested cicadas in the night biome. SND05 covers local audio lifecycle/volume; G01/R01 preserve simulation and race behavior; Q01/V06 cover verification and mobile acceptance.
 
 Night (`night_city`) races now play one recorded cicada ambience voice, including the countdown and untimed practice. The 18-second mono loop fades in/out over 0.75 seconds at a restrained level, pauses with the race and application, restarts on retry, stops when switching away from night, and is freed with the race. It follows the existing Vehicle volume and master mute. No menu labels/settings were added. Music, vehicle clips, weather behavior, canonical physics, inputs and race contracts are unchanged.
@@ -37,3 +39,29 @@ Initial failures retained in command history: restricted network socket and Godo
 Review checkpoint: [task-only patch](evidence/night-cicadas-2026-10-09/review-checkpoint.patch), created against the exact pre-task core/document content and including the new audio asset. Unrelated workspace edits are preserved.
 
 Phone attachment was not checked; no phone/device audio test, Android export/install, full Validate, deployment or production action occurred. Remaining acceptance: owner listening for cicada character/volume against engine and music, actual phone speakers/headphones/Bluetooth, background/foreground and pause/retry on device, and mobile memory/performance. Desktop digital continuity does not establish those results.
+
+## Less conspicuous looping, 2026-10-10
+
+SND19/SND05/G01/R01/Q01/V06: owner reports that the night cicada loop is too easy to notice. The previous linear overlap had a periodic volume dip: its quietest 250-ms overlap window was 3.72 dB below the whole-clip RMS. The new master retains 2–46 seconds of the same original field recording and uses a four-second cosine/sine equal-power overlap. It repeats after 40 seconds rather than 18; the quietest overlap window is now 0.80 dB below whole-clip RMS. Full-source frequency filtering precedes the cut, avoiding artificial FFT edge wrapping at the edit. Natural insect variation remains; this is still a finite loop, not nonrepeating procedural ambience.
+
+The overall authored RMS stays at -22 dBFS and playback gain stays at 0.4. The asset is 3,528,044 bytes, up from 1,587,644 (1,940,400 additional PCM bytes before runtime copies); mono/44.1 kHz/16-bit and the one-voice runtime are unchanged. Source SHA-256 remains `6604bf85f17a5b88f68c64b71a48917d9679b96ec4a7d3aac984b73bea0f3261`; reproducible derivative SHA-256 is `d4baf926786113b59780bb7c9778e1ce1ec3f02442348ec2797b263443af806b`. No new source, runtime dependency, UI or simulation change.
+
+Changed files: `scripts/build_night_ambience.py`, `game/assets/audio/ambience/{night_cicadas.wav,manifest.json,NOTICE.txt}`, `game/tests/test_night_ambience.gd`, `scripts/review_night_ambience.py`, this document, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md` and `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md`. The focused test now checks the extended duration and captures two full playback cycles. PCM review compares the old/new overlap envelope, checks unchanged loudness and retains the native continuity/silence checks.
+
+Actual commands:
+
+```powershell
+python scripts/build_night_ambience.py
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action Import
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_night_ambience.gd
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command "& ./scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_night_ambience.gd -Graphical -TestArgument @('--capture')"
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestApp
+python scripts/build_night_ambience.py
+python scripts/review_night_ambience.py
+```
+
+The initial restricted importer failed reading the Windows certificate store; the authorized normal-access import succeeded. Initial native capture stopped at about 34 seconds after desktop focus loss, correctly producing zero observed wraps and failing the no-dropout assertion. Its [log](evidence/night-cicadas-loop-2026-10-10/initial-focus-interrupted.log) and [audio](evidence/night-cicadas-loop-2026-10-10/initial-focus-interrupted.wav) are retained. The capture fixture now explicitly delivers foreground notifications and presents the ambience each frame, matching a sustained foreground race; the separate pause/background assertions and production focus behavior remain intact.
+
+Final outcomes with pinned Godot 4.7.2 through `scripts/dev.ps1`: import passed, headless **25/25**, native **31/31** with two observed wraps, app **99/99**, PCM review **22/22**; a repeat offline build reproduced the exact derivative hash. [Native 81.003-second capture](evidence/night-cicadas-loop-2026-10-10/cicadas-two-wraps.wav): peak 0.193756, RMS 0.031540, minimum 100-ms RMS 0.026047. [Paused](evidence/night-cicadas-loop-2026-10-10/paused.wav), [muted](evidence/night-cicadas-loop-2026-10-10/muted.wav) and [finished](evidence/night-cicadas-loop-2026-10-10/finished.wav) output are digitally silent after drain. [PCM measurements](evidence/night-cicadas-loop-2026-10-10/pcm-review.json), command logs and [task-only Git patch](evidence/night-cicadas-loop-2026-10-10/task-review.patch) retain the evidence; unrelated workspace edits are preserved. No visible UI changed, so audio evidence replaces screenshots.
+
+Phone attachment was not checked; no device listening/test, Android export/install, full Validate, physics/backend change or deployment occurred. Remaining acceptance: owner judges whether repetition is sufficiently unobtrusive in a complete night race; actual phone/tablet speakers, headphones and Bluetooth; device lifecycle and the larger PCM asset's memory behavior. Digital continuity and reduced envelope dips do not establish subjective listening acceptance.
